A||N||1||Mankind||HELP - fragged tranny??||||9||
Z||000000||Mankind||07-22-2000||09:01 AM||||I have an '85 GT with the Muncie 3.65:1 4-speed manual.<P>I was just driving along all normal and pussyfooted like I usually do, and left a stop sign.  As I proceeded to shift into 2nd, I found that I couldn't.  The shifter would not go in.  I tried to shove it back in 1st, and I finally did, but the whole transaxle started to quake and an awful rough noise was coming from it.  I pulled over, turned the car off, put it in Reverse - the only way I could do it w/o grinding - and started it back up.  Same deal.  Awful shake and awful noise.  I limped to the nearest open lot and found that I couldn't get it to go into ANY gear at all.  I let the car cool and 30min later proceeded to shove it into 1st, where it ran awful again.  Stopped the car, tried it again, and found that now it would go into any gear way easily... but you could let the clutch fully out and nothing would happen.<P>My dad guessed the flywheel shattered.<P>1) What broke,<BR>2) who can sell me the answer to 1),<BR>3) how the hell do you install the answer to 1)???????<P>I'm a "starving college student" who just landed a full-time job 45min away and need to transport myself there to make cash for school... I can't have this car down for any amount of time.  Advice... puh-leeze!<BR><P>------------------<BR>--Adam Wosneski||||reg||9
Z||000001||Taijiguy||07-22-2000||10:40 AM||||This sucks, but it's all I can think of:<P>If the noise you were talking about happens with the engine running,  regardless of whether or not you have it in gear, clutch engaged or disengaged, then your dad might be right, it could be clutch related. <BR>If the noise only occured when you had the clutch released, regardless of the gear it was in, I'd say you are looking at a transaxle problem. And it could be any number of things. They are rebuildable, but as cheap as you can find one here on the board, you probably would be better off buying a replacement. <P>Sorry about your breakdown...although probably not what you wanted to read, I hope this info helps some.<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
